plugin-qualify (0.6.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Changelog: the per-rate soak verdict, the timedOut soak and the
    cost-field refusal (#32)
  * The cost gate refuses a reading missing a field it judges
    (hosting.cost.fields-missing) (#32)
  * A soak failure measured at the console's rate is unsuitable at that rate;
    a supervisor timeout is timedOut, never died (#32)
  * Changelog: the faithful measuring host and the worker in benchmark.py
    (#32)
  * benchmark.py: run the plugin's worker between blocks instead of dropping
    its jobs (#32)
  * lv2_measure: a faithful host - a real worker, patch:Set, a bounded soak
    sweep, a stdout of its own (#32)
  * Read the measurer's record past a plugin's banner, size a soak's limit,
    declare the soak sweep bounds (#32)
  * Version 0.6.0 (#32)
  * Parity test: keep openmixer's copy in the tree, held to its blob ids (#32)
  * Docs: the LV2 measurer, where it is found, and its parity test (#32)
  * npm release: install lilv and the LV2 headers before the native build
    (#32)
  * Packaging dry run: measure the LV2 fixtures through the installed package
    with nothing set (#32)
  * CI: install lilv and the LV2 headers the measurer builds against (#32)
  * Install the LV2 measurer beside the CLAP prober in the RPM and the DEB
    (#32)
  * lv2-measure.mjs measures the hosting dimensions through the native
    measurer (#32)
  * One declared list of the native tools, each found by its setting, then
    installed, then native/build (#32)
  * Test the LV2 measurer prints what openmixer's copy prints, byte for byte
    (#32)
  * native: take in the LV2 measurer's features oracle, and run it and the
    measurer in the tests (#32)
  * native: LV2 fixture bundles, an RT-safe and an RT-unsafe gain (#32)
  * native: take in openmixer's LV2 measurer and host probe (#32)

 -- Pau Aliagas <linuxnow@gmail.com>  Tue, 13 Oct 2026 08:13:01 +0000
